Why This Works: [1-2 sentences on the psychological reason this pattern retains viewers]

Why Suitable For This Content: [1-2 sentences on why this specific Shloka's content fits this pattern]

Beat Sequence: [4 beats total]

For each beat provide:

— Beat number and time range [e.g., Beat 1 — 0:00 to 0:15]

— Purpose of this beat

— [MM:SS] "Exact verbatim words"

— Audio Cue: [Suggest music shifts, drops, or SFX for the editor]

— Visual Suggestion: [Speaker close-up / full-screen text / B-roll description based on Visual Setup input]

— On-screen text (if any): "Exact verbatim words only — max 3-4 words from the line" [MM:SS]. If no 3-4 word phrase from the line works as standalone on-screen text, write: [None — no extract works standalone]. Never paraphrase for on-screen text.

End each approach with:

Strength: [What makes this approach powerful]

Risk: [Specifically — what type of viewer might click away, and at which beat]

Step 3 — Self-Score

After generating all 3 approaches, score each on these 4 parameters, each out of 5:

Immediate Personal Reaction — will Beat 1 make a mobile viewer stop within 3 seconds?

Emotional Progression — do the 4 beats feel emotionally different from each other?

Lean-In Strength — does Beat 4 create genuine curiosity that cannot be resolved without watching?

Verbatim Quality — are the chosen lines conversationally strong, not just philosophically correct? Score 5 if: line is under 15 words, contains a recognizable emotion or relatable situation, uses first-person or direct address, and is grammatically complete as a standalone sentence. Deduct 1 point for each criterion missed.

Present scores in a comparison table — this is the only permitted use of tables in this output.

Total score out of 20.

Priority Flag Assignment:
The highest scoring approach gets 🔴. If two approaches score within 2 points of each other, both get 🔴 and flag them as: [Tied — both worth A/B testing]. The remaining approach gets 🟢. No two approaches may share 🟡. 🟡 is assigned only when exactly one approach is a clear second — not tied with 🔴 and clearly above 🟢.

Recommend the highest scoring approach. If flagged as a tie, recommend both for A/B testing.

